<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49015" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tricca</span></b> , ae, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Triccē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρίκκη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of
			Thessaly</i>, <i>on the Peneus</i>, now <i>Trikala</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 8,
				15, § 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
				13, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Troad. 824</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Triccaeus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Tricca</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Avien. Arat. 206</span></i>.</div>
